cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "KaRMA: Kinematic Rolling Manipulation Ability"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Peticco
    given-names: Martin
    affiliation: "Massachusetts Institute of Technology"
  - family-names: Agrawal
    given-names: Pulkit
    affiliation: "Massachusetts Institute of Technology"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mfpeticco/karma-hand-metric"
abstract: >-
  A kinematics-only metric for fine manipulation ability in robotic hands.
  KaRMA quantifies the reachable in-hand translation and reorientation of a
  spherical test object held in a two-finger precision pinch, under feasible
  rolling motions that maintain contact.
